INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (1, 1, 3, 'SPRINT 6: you own unit 1 — Core engine, RST.Core/Telemetry (spec doc 5, Build Plan step 1: envelope + event models, JSONL serializer, OutboxWriter + bounded queue, prefs store, RecoveryScanner, RetentionPruner, unit tests; zero Revit/UI refs — enforced by project refs). Nothing depends on your start; unit 3 (DEV2) and unit 2 (you) depend on your merge; REV1 reviews you. Load the sprint skill and take your slot. First move: start now. Units 2 (collector, after 1) and 5 (consent, after 2+4) are also yours — task rows will follow as they unblock.', '2026-07-18 18:18:52', '2026-07-18 18:19:34', 'task', 'ee34635f029d49cea593aee13e57102a');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (2, 1, 4, 'SPRINT 6: you own unit 3 — Aggregator, RST.Core/Telemetry (spec doc 5, Build Plan step 3: per-day open-hours series, open/sync event series, current-file matching, synthetic-outbox tests). Depends on unit 1 (DEV1) — core event models; unit 4 (Activity tab, also yours) depends on you; REV1 reviews you. Load the sprint skill and take your slot. First move: wait for unit 1''s merge — you''ll get a task row when it lands.', '2026-07-18 18:18:52', '2026-07-18 19:23:05', 'task', '223f5ccef4d84a33be6000bc428a8461');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (3, 1, 5, 'SPRINT 6: you review units 1–5 (spec doc 5, telemetry v1) — Major/Medium block, Low goes to the unit report. Load the sprint skill (reviewer slot). Review requests come to you directly as units go green.', '2026-07-18 18:18:52', '2026-07-18 18:40:33', 'task', '5b0c1b321c494c778ffe58344c8df921');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (4, 3, 1, 'sprint 6: unit 1 building — branch pending, base df387c7', '2026-07-18 18:19:34', '2026-07-18 18:20:07', 'result', 'd44bd805bbad44629616b54c188d616a');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (5, 3, 1, 'sprint 6: unit 1 pr-open — PR #100 (feat/telemetry-core)', '2026-07-18 18:35:13', '2026-07-18 18:35:52', 'result', '3fefff37eb384852abf34144090fb21b');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (6, 3, 5, 'sprint 6: unit 1 ready for review — PR #100, checks green (6/6)

Core engine (RST.Core/Telemetry) per spec doc 5 Build Plan step 1: envelope + event models, JSONL serializer, OutboxWriter + bounded queue, prefs store, InstallIdStore, RecoveryScanner, RetentionPruner, 25 unit tests. Zero Revit/UI refs.

Open ambiguity calls (gate against these readings, not your own guess):
- ambiguity: spec says failures "log once to Serilog" but RST.Core has no Serilog ref → chose injectable Action<string> log callback; unit 2 wires it to Serilog — keeps the fork-liftable core dependency-free.
- ambiguity: "existing OverrideRootForTests pattern extended to cover them" → chose a separate OverrideTelemetryRootForTests hook — TelemetryRoot resolves to LocalAppData, not the roaming Root, so one override for both would conflate scopes.
- ambiguity: doc_closed status semantics for recovery''s open-doc replay unspecified → chose Cancelled/Failed = doc still open (gets synthetic close), missing/other status = closed.
- ambiguity: recovery of a file with zero parseable lines unspecified → chose synthetic session_end anyway, session_guid from the {install}_{session}.jsonl filename, ts from file mtime — upholds the closed-file contract for every non-live file.
- ambiguity: "probe by attempting an exclusive append-open" → probe opens FileAccess.Write/FileShare.None; on Windows a reader-held file also probes locked (spec wants those skipped anyway); verified the probe conflicts with the writer''s advisory lock on Linux so CI exercises lock-skip for real.', '2026-07-18 18:37:39', '2026-07-18 18:47:28', 'shell', '1c436f094cd94bb68775b49092684058');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (7, 3, 1, 'sprint 6: unit 1 in-review — PR #100 checks green 6/6, review requested from REV1 (5 ambiguity calls in the request)', '2026-07-18 18:37:39', '2026-07-18 18:38:48', 'result', 'b0751e78ab8342409bcefcfb13d8be1c');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (8, 1, 1, 'pr_event jedbjorn/rst-c#100: checks green (SUCCESS) @ 63d841d', '2026-07-18 18:38:09', '2026-07-18 18:39:18', 'pr_event', NULL);
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (9, 1, 3, 'SPRINT 6: ruling on unit 1''s five ambiguity calls — all five upheld as made (log-callback core, separate telemetry test override, Cancelled/Failed=still-open, filename+mtime recovery for unparseable orphans, write-exclusive probe). No changes needed; they''re logged on the board. Unit 2 note: wire the collector''s log callback to Serilog as you proposed.', '2026-07-18 18:38:48', '2026-07-18 18:58:53', 'task', '550b2ed3ff314529b2642ed8e1e98532');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (10, 5, 3, 'Sprint 6 unit 1 review: CHANGES REQUIRED — 1 Major, 5 Medium.

SC-016 (Major) — TelemetryPrefs.cs:43-60 fails open on corrupt/unreadable/truncated JSON (Enabled=true) and writes non-atomically/with thrown IO. This contradicts spec §Threading & Safety (corrupt prefs/IO => telemetry off) and disabled-state persistence. Missing file may default on; damaged/unreadable existing state must fail closed. Make persistence crash-safe and add negative/error tests; replace the current test that asserts corrupt => enabled.

SC-017 (Medium) — RetentionPruner.cs:47 calls AddDays(-retentionDays) outside the catch and accepts int.MaxValue, so corrupt but parseable prefs can throw despite Prune''s never-throws contract. Validate/bound the window and test the huge-positive branch.

SC-018 (Medium) — InstallIdStore.cs:30-45 is check-then-overwrite. Two simultaneous first-start Revit processes can mint A/B, both return different IDs, and the last writer wins. Use atomic create-if-absent with loser re-read/retry and add a concurrent-first-run test.

SC-019 (Medium) — TelemetryJson.cs:31-38 accepts any JSON containing event_type. RecoveryScanner.cs:65 and RetentionPruner.cs:55 then trust a malformed {event_type:session_end} as closed, skipping synthesis and eventually allowing orphan deletion. Validate the mandatory envelope/schema and test this negative path through recovery/prune.

SC-020 (Medium) — OutboxWriter.cs:84-94 invokes _log synchronously under _gate from Enqueue. With the ratified unit-2 Serilog wiring, queue overflow can perform/block on logging IO on Revit''s event thread, violating cheap capture + enqueue only. Defer the one-shot warning to the writer/background side and test it is not invoked synchronously by Enqueue.

SC-021 (Medium) — RecoveryScannerTests covers Cancelled and Succeeded only, but the ratified semantics also require Failed => still open and missing/other => closed. Add exact cases; both realistic regressions currently stay green.

Patch and re-push, keep all six checks green, then re-request review with these flag IDs.', '2026-07-18 18:47:28', '2026-07-18 18:58:53', 'shell', '68749b4ccf6a47ae9fb436cacfd9ac91');
