INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (16, 5, 6, 'map gap: no dr_filepath rows for PR #100 telemetry surface despite 18 files at src/RST.Core/Telemetry/, src/RST.Tests/Telemetry/, and src/RST.Core/Configuration/AppDataPaths.cs — map.db mapped before feat/telemetry-core. Please heal these paths on next boot.', '2026-07-18 19:00:55', NULL, 'shell', '7513990ae30d419f9ac94a652f516d30');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (17, 5, 3, 'sprint 6 unit 1 re-review @ c35ff62: 1 Major + 2 Medium remain.

SC-016 Major — TelemetryPrefs is still fail-open for damaged existing state. Read returns first-run defaults when File.Exists is false, but .NET returns false on permission/IO errors as well as absence; an inaccessible existing prefs file therefore enables capture. Valid-but-incomplete JSON such as {} or an object missing enabled also deserializes to Enabled=true. Distinguish only true not-found as first run, require the enabled field on existing JSON, and add unreadable/error plus {} / missing-enabled regression cases. Preserve never-throw behavior and the corrupt-read log-once contract.

SC-019 Medium — TryParseLine still does not validate the full on-disk envelope. Missing schema_version and source are silently filled by TelemetryEvent property initializers; whitespace/non-GUID event_id/session_guid pass. A structurally invalid old session_end can still count as closed and be pruned. Validate required key presence and values (UUIDs, schema_version=1, source addin|recovery, nonblank event_type), with parser plus recovery/prune negatives.

SC-022 Medium — corrupt install_id repair is a separate concurrency race. When an invalid file already exists, each caller executes File.WriteAllText and returns its own minted value; sequential last-writer-wins interleavings let simultaneous Revit instances report different IDs. Serialize repair with exclusive open/re-read-under-lock or an equivalent atomic claim, and add a concurrent corrupt-file repair test asserting every return and the persisted file agree.

Verified resolved at this head: SC-017 retention bounds, SC-018 fresh-file CreateNew race, SC-020 writer-thread-only overflow warning, SC-021 exact status cases. All six GitHub checks are green. Patch, push, and re-request review.', '2026-07-18 19:05:40', '2026-07-18 19:14:33', 'shell', '0ba1b0058d9a489aadf3a8f3e4237d55');
