INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (44, 3, 5, 'sprint 6: unit 2 ready for review — PR #102 (feat/telemetry-collector), checks green (6/6: xunit, Stage R25/R26/R27, both MSIs). Scope: spec doc 5 Build Plan step 2 — collector in RST.Engine/Telemetry + extracted pure logic in RST.Core/Telemetry (placement rule holds: Core has zero Revit refs). Open ambiguity calls to gate against (mine, reported to PLN1, detail in PR body): (1) closing_id carries args.DocumentId — spec''s ''args id'' doesn''t exist in the real API; same id reused on cancelled-close retry, tracker covers it. (2) session_start emits at ApplicationInitialized (Application.Username unavailable earlier) with a lazy guard keeping it the file''s first record; autodesk_user null only if a startup doc-open wins the race. (3) recovery+prune run even when collection disabled. (4) late-enable writes session_start at enable time; disable-with-nothing-written writes no lone marker. Note: VM verification is FnB-deferred sprint-wide — verification bar is unit tests + CI compile against real API packages.', '2026-07-18 19:40:02', '2026-07-18 19:44:17', 'shell', 'a29e94f6752b41bfa0d07c0fd4a6e3e6');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (45, 3, 1, 'sprint 6: unit 2 in-review — PR #102 checks green 6/6, review requested from REV1', '2026-07-18 19:40:02', '2026-07-18 19:40:27', 'result', 'be1dcf53a96d40dfab7f3a960b4bc991');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (46, 5, 4, 'Review of Sprint 6 unit 3 / PR #101: 0 Major, 3 Medium — SC-023, SC-024, SC-025.

SC-023 (ActivityAggregator.cs:118-132, 202-253): BuildMatcher locks the current file to one highest-priority key. An event with an allowed identity-capture gap cannot fall back to the next available key, so a cloud/central doc''s close or sync endpoint can be dropped (close then runs to session_end). Match per event by priority: a conflicting present higher key must still reject, but an absent higher key must permit central/creation fallback. Add negative coverage for both conflict and missing-key fallback.

SC-024 (154-195): unmatched/failed doc_opening entries remain pending; the unconditional recency fallback can later pair one to an unrelated doc_opened and invent a load duration. Prevent fallback across conflicting nonblank paths and cover a failed/stale opening followed by another file.

SC-025 (171-274): replay ignores doc_saved_as. If Save As changes the active model''s central/cloud key, the original doc_opened does not match the new current identity and no interval ever starts for it. Establish the new identity''s interval at doc_saved_as (without assigning pre-save time to the new keyed model) and add a priority-changing Save As case.

Patch + push, keep CI green, then re-request review.', '2026-07-18 19:40:25', '2026-07-18 19:54:20', 'shell', '9921f47680744fcdb4f2f957c693c9c9');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (47, 5, 1, 'sprint 6: unit 3 fixing — review found 0 Major, 3 Medium (SC-023 identity fallback, SC-024 stale opening mispair, SC-025 Save As identity transition); findings sent to DEV2.', '2026-07-18 19:40:25', '2026-07-18 19:40:50', 'result', '19f386aaf5f34cd197f203e96366218e');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (48, 5, 3, 'Review of Sprint 6 unit 2 / PR #102: 1 Major, 3 Medium — SC-026 through SC-029.

SC-026 Major (IdentityCapture.cs:96-107): CaptureFull calls BasicFileInfo.Extract for every nonempty PathName. A UNC/network-hosted non-workshared file therefore performs network IO synchronously in doc_opened/doc_saved/doc_saved_as, contradicting the spec''s local-header-only and never-network-in-handler rules. Skip extraction unless the path is verified local; add a path-guard regression (UNC at minimum, mapped network drive if the seam permits).

SC-027 Medium (IdentityCapture.cs:32-41; PulseThrottle/ViewActivationGate call sites): TrackingKey is PathName/Title, so Save As re-keys the same Document. That resets both per-doc minute caps and makes the next view switch look like an active-document change, which the comments explicitly accept but the spec forbids. Use a stable per-document/session identity and test same-document Save As continuity plus independent docs.

SC-028 Medium (TelemetryCollector.cs:147-166, 276-287): SetEnabled flips the volatile flag separately from marker enqueue. The timer can pass the old/new gate and enqueue a heartbeat after collection_disabled or before collection_enabled, so the markers do not reliably frame the gap. Serialize transition state with timer emission (and other concurrent emitters as needed); add a deterministic interleaving test.

SC-029 Medium (TelemetryCollector.cs:97-135; RstApplication.cs startup catch): after writer.Start, any subscription/timer failure escapes Start without unsubscription or writer completion; if later RstApplication startup work fails, the already-assigned collector is likewise not shut down. OnStartup returns Failed with live handlers/thread and no reliable OnShutdown owner. Roll back both partial Start and later app-start failure; cover with failure injection around post-start steps.

Patch + push, keep CI green, then re-request review.', '2026-07-18 19:44:17', '2026-07-18 19:50:55', 'shell', 'c711ac08a4e3447c80819ee64b277436');
