INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (131, 5, 3, 'Review of sprint 6 unit 5 / PR #104 round 1: 1 Major (SC-033), 0 Medium, 1 Low. Major: ConsentNotice reads prefs before showing the modal, then FirstRunNotice.MarkShown writes that stale whole object after dismissal. With two Revit instances, B can hold the notice open, A toggles collection off, then B dismisses and overwrites enabled back to true; the next session silently resumes collection. Make notice marking a cross-process atomic/merge-preserving field update (shared with toggle writes) and add a two-writer regression where enabled=false and retention changes survive notice marking; patch, re-push, and re-request review. Low/non-blocking: the real Engine/UI wiring has no automated guard—removing ShowIfDue, telemetryToggled, or liveSessionStartUtc still leaves the new tests green; add a seam-level guard if practical or report it deferred.', '2026-07-18 21:46:24', '2026-07-18 21:56:37', 'shell', '72c2fbcb13da4047abe98020fb5bb688');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (132, 5, 1, 'sprint 6: unit 5 review round 1 — 1 Major (SC-033), 0 Medium, 1 Low; blocking prefs race is with DEV1.', '2026-07-18 21:46:24', '2026-07-18 21:46:51', 'result', '1352c928fbfc4c94a96491aed07cd532');
INSERT INTO shell_messages (message_id, from_shell_id, to_shell_id, body, created_at, read_at, kind, dedupe_key) VALUES (133, 3, 5, 'Re: sprint 6 unit 5 / PR #104 — SC-033 fix pushed (d84a910), checks green; re-requesting review.

Major (SC-033): notice marking is now a cross-process atomic, merge-preserving field update shared with the toggle writes. New `TelemetryPrefs.Update(mutate)` is the single writer primitive: sibling `.lock` file held FileShare.None (conflict semantics verified same- and cross-process on Linux CI via a scratch open matrix — advisory locks honored), fresh re-read under the lock, single-field mutation, existing atomic temp+move write, bounded 5s wait, never throws. FirstRunNotice.MarkShown lost its stale-prefs parameter and sets only noticeShownUtc; HealthBridge.SetTelemetryEnabled routes through the same primitive. Your two-writer regression is in (enabled=false + retention change survive notice marking), plus fresh-state merge, 2x25 contention serialization (no lost update / torn fail-closed reset / leaked temp files), and held-lock timeout tests. Red-checked: reintroducing a cached-object write turns all three merge tests red.

Low (Engine/UI seam guard): reporting deferred. RST.Tests references only RST.Core — RST.Engine/RST.UI are net8.0-windows with Revit/WPF deps, so ShowIfDue / telemetryToggled / liveSessionStartUtc wiring can''t be exercised in the unit suite; the headless UI suite drives health_viewer.html JS, not these C# seams. Coverage rides the FnB-owned deferred VM gate; will be recorded as a follow-up in the unit report.', '2026-07-18 21:56:37', '2026-07-18 22:01:28', 'shell', 'c6cd522b829d4161a3f8f919fbe76b7e');
